  intro_message = coalesce(intro_message, $$Thanks for connecting, Isaac. I am interested in how SH/FT is managing the gap between a strong strategic growth model and the hands-on campaign, data, automation, and measurement work required to operationalize it consistently across clients. I have led that connective work across CRM, marketing automation, customer databases, analytics, forecasting, and activation, while my partner Harsh brings deeper data architecture and modeling. I would be glad to compare approaches and explore where complementary fractional capacity could reduce delivery friction. Our framework is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach$$),
  follow_up_message = coalesce(follow_up_message, $$Isaac, one challenge I frequently see is that teams can define the desired customer experience and technology future state before they have settled the lifecycle definitions, decision rules, data ownership, and operating cadence needed to make it real. A useful discussion may be how SH/FT bridges that layer across strategy, implementation, and measurable client outcomes.$$)
